# WHAT ALREADY EXISTS AND IS DEPLOYED:**

```
✅ Cloud Run Express server — live
✅ GitHub, LinkedIn, API proxy — connected
✅ ChatGPT, Claude, Notion — connected
✅ app.akilah — connects to Cloud Run
✅ webapp.akilah — connects to app.akilah
✅ client.akilah — single entry point
✅ Gateway — working
✅ Firebase — Realtime DB connected, writes confirmed
✅ staging.akilah — sections defined (intake → deconstruction
     → review → decision → publish → rework)
✅ Session capsule design — done
✅ Governance + policy binding — done
✅ Capabilities — built
✅ Common files / templates — done
✅ Memory.db — exists with script_registry, tool_registry
✅ script_intelligence.py — exists (has one syntax error at line 863)
✅ AkilahAgent.py — compiles, CLI commands working
✅ Governance framework scripts — exist
✅ session_db_logger.py — exists
✅ PathSelector.py — exists
✅ shared_state.py — exists
```

---

**WHAT WE ARE WORKING ON — THE NEW SYSTEM:**

```
01 → WIRE EVERYTHING TO THE NEW SYSTEM
     Everything already built needs to connect
     to the new .akilah architecture
     Not rebuilding — rewiring

02 → SESSION AS A CONTAINER
     Every session = one complete self-contained file
     Holds: data + alignment + governance
             + security + state + accessibility
     Backed up to Firebase
     Format-agnostic (file or DB or both)

03 → CAPABILITIES OVER SCRIPTS
     Stop calling scripts
     Start calling named capabilities
     Dynamic actions configured into
     the session container

04 → STAGING = THE SESSION BRAIN + AI BRIDGE
     Active session holds everything
     Staging = controlled window for AI
     Workspace = scoped view for you
     You designate what AI sees
     AI works only in its slice

05 → APP.AKILAH = ONE ENDPOINT OS
     Single entry for ANY AI
     (Claude, ChatGPT, Copilot, MCP, CLI)
     client.akilah loads capabilities dynamically
     No new integration per AI model
     Gateway authenticates
     app.akilah executes on behalf

06 → ENTRY MARKERS ON ALL .AKILAH FILES
     Every file declares itself
     Four parts: narrative + container
                + actions + execution gate
     One script reads any file the same way

07 → ALIGNMENT + GOVERNANCE BAKED IN
     Into staging
     Into client.akilah
     Not separate — inside the session container
```

---

**THE FOUR AI PROBLEMS BEING SOLVED:**

```
01 → Runtime context alignment
     → staging holds the persistent brain

02 → Intelligence alignment
     → governance baked into session + markers

03 → Safe execution
     → one script, one process, approval gates

04 → No place that brings it all together
     → app.akilah + .akilah language = the OS
```

