---

webapp.akilah
  → shell only
  → loads workspace.akilah via app.akilah
        ↓
workspace.akilah
  → loads components into containers
  → containers filled by app.akilah (the connector)
  → data comes from staging (the session)
        ↓
THE SESSION FLOW (all inside staging):
  01 → intake        (what you're trying to achieve)
  02 → deconstruction (breaking it down)
  03 → clarification  (what we're doing RIGHT NOW)
  04 → insight        (what we learned)
  05 → to-do          (what needs to happen next)
---

AI is stateless by design
  → forgets what was said 10 min ago
  → gets confused when too much is in context
  → makes mistakes because it lost the thread

Human has to hold everything cognitively
  → exhausting
  → error-prone
  → breaks the flow

WORKSPACE = your controlled slice viewer
  → you pull specific slices FROM staging
  → you see only what you chose to surface
  → you designate which slices AI can see
  → AI only works in its designated slice
  → AI cannot see outside what you gave it
---

APP.AKILAH = the slicer
  ACTIVE SESSION (you hold everything)
        ↓ you decide what AI needs to see
  STAGING (AI's controlled slice)
        ↓ back-and-forth happens here
        ↓ clarification, deconstruction, review
        ↓ approved
  ACTIVE SESSION (result committed back)
        ↓ when read
  insight: workspace is a scoped view into staging
          — you see one stage at a time
          — the rest is held, not shown
  to-do: design the staging sections so each stage
        is a discrete, loadable container
        that workspace can surface independently
---

workspace.akilah
  ├── active session view   → your full picture
  └── staging view          → AI's slice
        → you can switch between them
        → staging is what you control and send
        → session is what you hold
